led with p, and arrows to s2 and back from s1. State s1 has an arrow to s2 and back to s0, with \the label q on the arrow to s1. State s2 has an arrow to s3 labeled with p and q. State s3 has a loop arrow back to itself labeled with an empty set symbol, indicating no further transitions. The chart illustrates how the system moves between states based\ on inputs p and q, showing possible paths and conditions for each transition.␀)/K 15/P 34567 0 R/Pg 1423 0 R/S/Figure/Type/StructElem>>endobj34605 0 obj<</K 4/P 34567 0 R/Pg 1423 0 R/S/Caption/Type/StructElem>>endobj34606 0 obj<</A<</BBox[282.635955 542.463012 353.423948 606.947996]/O/Layout>>/Alt(A tree diagram illustrating a hierarchical relationship starting from a top node labeled with the number 1. This node branches into two main parts: the left branch leads to a node labeled "EU" with the number 2, and the right branch leads to a node labele\d "AG" with the number 5. From "EU," two branches extend downward to nodes labeled "p" with the number 3 and "q" with the number 4. From "AG," a branch leads to a node labeled "EF" with the number 6, which further branches down to a node labeled "q" with \the number 7. The diagram shows a structured flow from the top node through labeled nodes, indicating a sequence or classification where "EU" and "AG" are key intermediate points leading to final elements "p," "q," and "EF," with "EF" further leading to "\q." This structure helps visualize relationships or decision paths among these elements.␀)/K 16/P 34567 0 R/Pg 1423 0 R/S/Figure/Type/StructElem>>endobj34607 0 obj<</K 6/P 34567 0 R/Pg 1423 0 R/S/Caption/Type/StructElem>>endobj34608 0 obj<</K 14/P 34567 0 R/Pg 1423 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj34609 0 obj<</K 8/P 34567 0 R/Pg 1423 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj34610 0 obj<</K[9 34872 0 R 11]/P 34567 0 R/Pg 1423 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj34611 0 obj<</K[13<</MCID 0/Pg 1440 0 R/Type/MCR>><</MCID 1/Pg 1440 0 R/Type/MCR>><</MCID 2/Pg 1440 0 R/