s that not diamond false holds. Below these, four rules of inference are shown: axiom rule states th\at if phi is an instance of an axiom, then phi holds; elimination rule states that if phi is in the set gamma, then phi holds; necessitation rule states that if phi holds, then box phi holds; and modus ponens states that if phi and phi implies psi hold, t\hen psi holds. This collection defines the foundational logical principles and inference steps for constructing valid proofs in a formal system.␀)/K 2/P 36454 0 R/Pg 1294 0 R/S/Figure/Type/StructElem>>endobj36486 0 obj<</K[3 37575 0 R 37576 0 R 157 158 37577 0 R 159 160]/P 36454 0 R/Pg 1294 0 R/S/Caption/Type/StructElem>>endobj36487 0 obj<</K[10 37569 0 R 13 37570 0 R 16 37571 0 R 19 37572 0 R 22 37573 0 R 25 37574 0 R 28]/P 36454 0 R/Pg 1294 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj36488 0 obj<</K 29/P 36454 0 R/Pg 1294 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj36489 0 obj<</K[161 162 37566 0 R 37567 0 R 33]/P 36454 0 R/Pg 1294 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj36490 0 obj<</K 35/P 36454 0 R/Pg 1294 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj36491 0 obj<</K[38 37541 0 R 41 37542 0 R 44 37543 0 R 47 37544 0 R 50 37545 0 R 53 37546 0 R 56 37547 0 R 59 37548 0 R 61 37549 0 R 63 37550 0 R 65 37551 0 R 68 37552 0 R 71 37553 0 R 74 37554 0 R 79 37555 0 R 81 37556 0 R 84 37557 0 R 87 37558 0 R 90 37559 0 R 93]/P 36454 0 R/Pg 1294 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj36492 0 obj<</K[95 37539 0 R 98 37540 0 R]/P 36454 0 R/Pg 1294 0 R/S/H2/Type/StructElem>>endobj36493 0 obj<</K[103 37517 0 R 37518 0 R 163 164 37519 0 R 165 166 37520 0 R 112 37521 0 R 115 37522 0 R 117 37523 0 R 120 37524 0 R 123 37525 0 R 126 37526 0 R 129 37527 0 R 132 37528 0 R 135 37529 0 R 138 37530 0 R 141 37531 0 R 144 37532 0 R 147 37533 0 R 150 37534 0 R 153 37535 0 R 156]/P 36454 0 R/Pg 1294 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj36494 0 obj<</A 37516 0 R/Alt(This collection presents logical rules used in formal proofs, showing how different statements lead to conclusions. Each rule uses Greek letters and symbols to represent logical expressions and their relationships. The rules are grouped by the type of log\ical operation they involve, such as conjunction \(and\), disjunction \(or\), implication \(if-then\), and modal operators \(box and diamond\). Each rule shows premises above a line and the conclusion below, indicating how to derive the conclusion from th\e premises. The purpose is to guide step-by-step reasoning in logic, helping to prove complex statements from simpler ones. The notation includes small and capital Greek letters, logical connectives like "and," "or," "implies," and modal operators, with s\ubscripts and superscripts clarifying specific cases or conditions. This set is important for understanding how formal logical arguments are constructed and verified.␀)/K 2/P 36454 0 R/Pg 1297 0 R/S/Figure/Type/StructElem>>endobj36495 0 obj<</K[3 37506 0 R 6 37507 0 R 9 37508 0 R 12 37509 0 R 15 37510 0 R 17 37511 0 R 19 37512 0 R 22 37513 0 R 25]/P 36454 0 R/Pg 1297 0 R/S/Caption/Type/StructElem>>endobj36496 0 obj<</K[26 37488 0 R 37489 0 R 29 37490 0 R 31 37491 0 R 34 37492 0 R 36 37493 0 R 39 37494 0 R 41 37495 0 R 46]/P 36454 0 R/Pg 1297 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj36497 0 obj<</Border[0 0 0]/K[48 37482 0 R 50 37483 0 R 52 37484 0 R]/P 36454 0 R/Pg 1297 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj36498 0 obj<</K[57 37478 0 R 60 37479 0 R 63 37480 0 R 66 37481 0 R 69]/P 36454 0 R/Pg 1297 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj36499 0 obj<</K[37465 0 R 73 37466 0 R 76 37467 0 R 79 37468 0 R 82 37469 0 R 84 37470 0 R 86 37471 0 R 88 37472 0 R 91 37473 0 R 93]/P 36454 0 R/Pg 1297 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj36500 0 obj<</K[1 37457 0 R 4 37458 0 R 7 37459 0 R 10 37460 0 R 12 37461 0 R 14 37462 0 R 17]/P 36454 0 R/Pg 1300 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj36501 0 obj<</K 19/P 36454 0 R/Pg 1300 0 R/S/H3/Type/StructElem>>endobj36502 0 obj<</K 21/P 36454 0 R/Pg 1300 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj36503 0 obj<</K[22 