 that if capital Gamma proves phi implies psi, then capital Gamma also proves box phi implies box psi. The second rule, labeled D, sa\ys that if capital Gamma proves phi, then capital Gamma proves diamond phi. The third rule, labeled T, states that if capital Gamma proves box phi, then capital Gamma proves phi. The fourth rule, labeled Nec, says that if phi is a theorem, then capital Ga\mma proves box phi. The fifth rule, labeled BI, states that if phi is in capital Gamma, then capital Gamma proves phi. The sixth rule, labeled MP, says that if capital Gamma proves phi implies psi and capital Gamma proves phi, then capital Gamma proves ps\i. These rules define how modal operators box and diamond interact with logical implication and provability.␀)/K 2/P 37809 0 R/Pg 1231 0 R/S/Figure/Type/StructElem>>endobj37838 0 obj<</K[30 31]/P 37809 0 R/Pg 1231 0 R/S/Caption/Type/StructElem>>endobj37839 0 obj<</K[32 34 35 38524 0 R]/P 37809 0 R/Pg 1231 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj37840 0 obj<</K 8/P 37809 0 R/Pg 1231 0 R/S/H3/Type/StructElem>>endobj37841 0 obj<</K 10/P 37809 0 R/Pg 1231 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj37842 0 obj<</K[11 38518 0 R 13 38519 0 R 15 38520 0 R 17]/P 37809 0 R/Pg 1231 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj37843 0 obj<</K 19/P 37809 0 R/Pg 1231 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj37844 0 obj<</K[36 37 38516 0 R]/P 37809 0 R/Pg 1231 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj37845 0 obj<</K 23/P 37809 0 R/Pg 1231 0 R/S/H3/Type/StructElem>>endobj37846 0 obj<</K[25 38514 0 R 27]/P 37809 0 R/Pg 1231 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj37847 0 obj<</K 28/P 37809 0 R/Pg 1231 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj37848 0 obj<</K[38 39 38512 0 R]/P 37809 0 R/Pg 1231 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj37849 0 obj<</K 1/P 37809 0 R/Pg 1234 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj37850 0 obj<</K 2/P 37809 0 R/Pg 1234 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj37851 0 obj<</K[38510 0 R 25 26]/P 37809 0 R/Pg 1234 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj37852 0 obj<</K 5/P 37809 0 R/Pg 