 variables, with arrows indicating logical implication or transformation, and square brackets denoting modal or operator contexts. This structured summary helps understand how complex logical expressions are matched and contained within certain sets, w\hich is important for formal verification or proof systems.␀)/K 2/P 37809 0 R/Pg 1258 0 R/S/Figure/Type/StructElem>>endobj37926 0 obj<</K 3/P 37809 0 R/Pg 1258 0 R/S/Caption/Type/StructElem>>endobj37927 0 obj<</K[4 38228 0 R 6 38229 0 R 8 38230 0 R 10 38231 0 R 12]/P 37809 0 R/Pg 1258 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj37928 0 obj<</K[13 38222 0 R 15 38223 0 R 17 38224 0 R 19]/P 37809 0 R/Pg 1258 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj37929 0 obj<</K[1 38220 0 R 3]/P 37809 0 R/Pg 1261 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj37930 0 obj<</K 4/P 37809 0 R/Pg 1261 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj37931 0 obj<</K[5 38207 0 R 7 38208 0 R 9 38209 0 R 38210 0 R]/P 37809 0 R/Pg 1261 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj37932 0 obj<</K[13 38203 0 R 15 38204 0 R 17]/P 37809 0 R/Pg 1261 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj37933 0 obj<</K[18 38201 0 R 20]/P 37809 0 R/Pg 1261 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj37934 0 obj<</K[21 38197 0 R 23 38198 0 R 25]/P 37809 0 R/Pg 1261 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj37935 0 obj<</K[63 64 38195 0 R]/P 37809 0 R/Pg 1261 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj37936 0 obj<</K[27 38176 0 R 29 38177 0 R 31 38178 0 R 33 38179 0 R 65 66 38180 0 R 67 68 38181 0 R 69 70 38182 0 R 41 38183 0 R 43]/P 37809 0 R/Pg 1261 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj37937 0 obj<</K[38156 0 R 38157 0 R]/P 37809 0 R/S/L/Type/StructElem>>endobj37938 0 obj<</A 38155 0 R/Alt(A logical rule showing how from three premises involving capital Pi prime, small omega, variables chi and phi, and capital Gamma, one can conclude a statement with capital Pi prime, a conditional from small phi to small psi, variable chi, and capital Gamm\a, all leading to capital Delta. The rule uses symbols for logical implication and boxes, indicating a step in a formal proof system.␀)/K 46/P 37809 0 R/Pg 1261 0 R/S/Figure/Type/StructElem>>endobj37939 0 obj<</K 38153 0 R/P 37809 0 R/S/P/T()/Type/StructElem>>endobj37940 0 obj<</A 38152 0 R/Alt(Capital Pi prime, comma small psi implies arrow to capital Chi, small phi, capital E sub small p superscript zero implies arrow to capital A sub small p superscript zero, small psi. Then a box operator followed by a negation symbol, capital Pi prime, comm\a small psi implies arrow to capital Chi, small phi, box operator negation capital E sub small p superscript zero implies arrow to small psi. Implies arrow to capital Pi prime, capital Chi, capital E sub small p superscript zero implies arrow to capital A\ sub small p superscript zero, all over capital Pi prime, open parenthesis small phi arrow to small psi close parenthesis implies arrow to capital Chi, capital E sub small p superscript zero implies arrow to capital A sub small p superscript zero. This ex\pression shows a logical or mathematical relationship involving implications between variables and operators, focusing on how certain conditions lead to conclusions about capital A sub small p superscript zero.␀)/K 50/P 37809 0 R/Pg 1261 0 R/S/Figure/Type/StructElem>>endobj37941 0 obj<</K 38150 0 R/P 37809 0 R/S/P/T()/Type/StructElem>>endobj37942 0 obj<</A 38149 0 R/Alt(Capital pi, capital gamma prime, comma, small psi turnstile to small chi, small phi implies capital delta, small psi, turnstile not capital pi, not capital gamma prime, small psi turnstile to small chi, small phi implies small psi, capital pi, capital gam\ma prime, small chi turnstile capital delta over capital pi, capital gamma, small phi implies small psi turnstile to small chi implies capital delta. This formula shows a logical rule combining three premises to conclude a final implication, illustrating \how complex logical statements can be derived step-by-step.␀)/K 6/P 37809 0 R/Pg 1264 0 R/S/Figure/Type/StructElem>>endobj37943 0 obj<</A 38148 0 R/Alt(Three related logical statements show how certain expressions involving capital Pi, capital E sub p, and capital A sub p transform under different conditions. The first states that if capital Pi and capital E sub p with inputs involving capital Gamma prim\e, psi, chi, and phi imply Delta, then capital A sub p with similar inputs also implies Delta. The second shows a similar implication but with a box operator applied to capital Gamma prime and psi, leading to capital A sub p with those inputs implying psi\. The third states that if capital Pi and capital E sub p with inputs capital Gamma prime and chi imply Delta, then capital A sub p with those inputs also implies Delta. These statements express how certain logical or mathematical properties are preserved\ or transferred between related expressions.␀)/K 16/P 37809 0 R/Pg 1264 0 R/S/Figure/Type/StructElem>>endobj37944 0 obj<</K 18/P 37809 0 R/Pg 1264 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj37945 0 obj<</K 20/P 37809 0 R/Pg 1264 0 R/S/H2/Type/StructElem>>endobj37946 0 obj<</K 22/P 37809 0 R/Pg 1264 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj37947 0 obj<</K[30 31 38146 0 R]/P 37809 0 R/Pg 1264 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj37948 0 obj<</K 24/P 37809 0 R/Pg 1264 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj37949 0 obj<</K[32 33 38144 0 R]/P 37809 0 R/Pg 1264 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj37950 0 obj<</K 27/P 37809 0 R/Pg 1264 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj37951 0 obj<</K 1/P 37809 0 R/Pg 1267 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj37952 0 obj<</K 3/P 37809 0 R/Pg 1267 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj37953 0 obj<</K[6 38135 0 R 40 42 44 46 48 49 38136 0 R 10]/P 37809 0 R/Pg 1267 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj37954 0 obj<</K[11 38127 0 R 13 38128 0 R 15 38129 0 R 17 38130 0 R 19]/P 37809 0 R/Pg 1267 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj37955 0 obj<</K 20/P 37809 0 R/Pg 1267 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj37956 0 obj<</K 22/P 37809 0 R/Pg 1267 0 R/S/H2/Type/StructElem>>endobj37957 0 obj<</K[24 38123 0 R 26 