 different types and states, such as child and adult, quiet and peaceful, using symbolic expressions. It sets conditions for when a child is considered quiet or peaceful based on factors like rain a\nd serving behavior. The expressions describe how states like peacefulness and quietness depend on each other and on external conditions, illustrating a system of logical dependencies and constraints. The purpose is to model and reason about these states \and their interactions in a formal way.␀)/K 2/P 38701 0 R/Pg 1174 0 R/S/Figure/Type/StructElem>>endobj38748 0 obj<</K 3/P 38701 0 R/Pg 1174 0 R/S/Caption/Type/StructElem>>endobj38749 0 obj<</K[4 39343 0 R 6 39344 0 R 8]/P 38701 0 R/Pg 1174 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj38750 0 obj<</K 10/P 38701 0 R/Pg 1174 0 R/S/H2/Type/StructElem>>endobj38751 0 obj<</K[12 39341 0 R 14]/P 38701 0 R/Pg 1174 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj38752 0 obj<</A 39340 0 R/Alt(The notation defines logical relationships between variables representing types and domains of children and adults, and their mappings. It shows conditions where certain child and adult types are equal or related, and how these relate to interpretation do\mains labeled CD, AD, and DA. The expressions also specify mappings between individuals named charly, agatha, serves, and others, indicating which child or adult type each corresponds to. This formalism is used to model and verify connections between diff\erent groups and their interpretations in a structured way.␀)/K 2/P 38701 0 R/Pg 1177 0 R/S/Figure/Type/StructElem>>endobj38753 0 obj<</K[3 39338 0 R 5]/P 38701 0 R/Pg 1177 0 R/S/Caption/Type/StructElem>>endobj38754 0 obj<</K 6/P 38701 0 R/Pg 1177 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj38755 0 obj<</K 8/P 38701 0 R/Pg 1177 0 R/S/H3/Type/StructElem>>endobj38756 0 obj<</K[10 39334 0 R 12 39335 0 R 14]/P 38701 0 R/Pg 1177 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj38757 0 obj<</K[15 39321 0 R 18 39322 0 R 21 39323 0 R 24 39324 0 R 27 39325 0 R 30 39326 0 R 33 