bj<</A 43479 0 R/Alt(The expression defines the absolute value of a function f at m, written as vertical bars around f sub m. It equals the absolute value of the cosine of the type of f if f is of type, and equals the absolute value of f otherwise. The second part defines the\ absolute value of f sub m as a piecewise function with three cases: if f is an integer function of v, it equals the absolute value of z sub small t; if f is a rational function of m, it equals the absolute value of q times the absolute value of b sub m t\imes m sub m; if f is a string function of x, it equals the absolute value of omega to the power of alpha. This notation explains how to calculate the absolute value depending on the type of function f, helping to understand different cases in a mathemati\cal or programming context.␀)/K[10 43480 0 R]/P 43473 0 R/Pg 798 0 R/S/Figure/Type/StructElem>>endobj43476 0 obj<</K[12 43477 0 R 14]/P 43473 0 R/Pg 798 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj43477 0 obj<</K 43478 0 R/P 43476 0 R/S/Reference/Type/StructElem>>endobj43478 0 obj<</Alt(Please refer Section 4 for your more information)/K[<</Obj 15023 0 R/Type/OBJR>>13]/P 43477 0 R/Pg 798 0 R/S/Link/Type/StructElem>>endobj43479 0 obj<</BBox[39.28 490.596997 386.403 730.493]/O/Layout/Placement/Block>>endobj43480 0 obj<</K 11/P 43475 0 R/Pg 798 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj43481 0 obj<</K 43484 0 R/P 43064 0 R/S/Reference/Type/StructElem>>endobj43482 0 obj<</K 43483 0 R/P 43064 0 R/S/Reference/Type/StructElem>>endobj43483 0 obj<</Alt(Please refer Section 2.3 for your more information)/K[<</Obj 15027 0 R/Type/OBJR>>5]/P 43482 0 R/Pg 798 0 R/S/Link/Type/StructElem>>endobj43484 0 obj<</Alt(Please refer Figure 3 your for more information)/K[<</Obj 15032 0 R/Type/OBJR>>3]/P 43481 0 R/Pg 798 0 R/S/Link/Type/StructElem>>endobj43485 0 obj<</K 43486 0 R/P 43059 0 R/S/Reference/Type/StructElem>>endobj43486 0 obj<</Alt(Please refer Figure 3 your for more information)/K[<</Obj 1501