es''; the latter sends an extended CNF to the SAT solver, which returns \an LRAT proof to ``verify LRAT''.\r\n␀)/K 2/P 48239 0 R/Pg 470 0 R/S/Figure/Type/StructElem>>endobj48292 0 obj<</K 3/P 48239 0 R/Pg 470 0 R/S/Caption/Type/StructElem>>endobj48293 0 obj<</K[4 49024 0 R 6 49025 0 R 12]/P 48239 0 R/Pg 470 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj48294 0 obj<</K 13/P 48239 0 R/Pg 470 0 R/S/H3/Type/StructElem>>endobj48295 0 obj<</K 15/P 48239 0 R/Pg 470 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj48296 0 obj<</K 18/P 48239 0 R/Pg 470 0 R/S/H4/Type/StructElem>>endobj48297 0 obj<</K 19/P 48239 0 R/Pg 470 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj48298 0 obj<</K 1/P 48239 0 R/Pg 473 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj48299 0 obj<</A 49022 0 R/Alt(Defines a function named small letter d sub small e sub small f sub small i sub small n sub small i sub small t sub small i sub small o sub small n sub small s sub small p sub small a sub small r sub small a sub small m sub small e sub small t sub small e\ sub small r squared that takes a simple graph with vertices from zero to n minus one as input and returns a proposition. The proposition states that for every pair of distinct vertices i and j, the adjacency between i and j in graph G is equivalent to th\e existence of a vertex k such that k is adjacent to i and k is adjacent to j. This expresses that an edge between i and j exists if and only if there is a common neighbor k connected to both i and j.)/K[2 49023 0 R]/P 48239 0 R/Pg 473 0 R/S/Figure/Type/StructElem>>endobj48300 0 obj<</K 5/P 48239 0 R/Pg 473 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj48301 0 obj<</K 6/P 48239 0 R/Pg 473 0 R/S/H3/Type/StructElem>>endobj48302 0 obj<</K 8/P 48239 0 R/Pg 473 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj48303 0 obj<</K 11/P 48239 0 R/Pg 473 0 R/S/H4/Type/StructElem>>endobj48304 0 obj<</K 12/P 48239 0 R/Pg 473 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj48305 0 obj<</A 49020 0 R/Alt(The statement presents a theorem about the iso-invariance of the law of the diameter in a specific mathematical setting. It says that for a group G acting on a space H, which is a simplicial graph, the law of the diameter of G is equal to the law of the d\iameter of H. This means the diameter measurement remains the same under the group action, showing a key property of invariance in this context.)/K[13 49021 0 R]/P 48239 0 R/Pg 473 0 R/S/Figure/Type/StructElem>>endobj48306 0 obj<</K 16/P 48239 0 R/Pg 473 0 R/S/H3/Type/StructElem>>endobj48307 0 obj<</K[18 49017 0 R 21 49018 0 R 24 49019 0 R 27]/P 48239 0 R/Pg 473 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj48308 0 obj<</K[28 49016 0 R 31]/P 48239 0 R/Pg 473 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj48309 0 obj<</K[32 49009 0 R 35 49010 0 R 38 49011 0 R 41 49012 0 R 44 49013 0 R 47 49014 0 R 50 49015 0 R 53]/P 48239 0 R/Pg 473 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj48310 0 obj<</K 1/P 48239 0 R/Pg 476 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj48311 0 obj<</K[2 49007 0 R 5 49008 0 R 8]/P 48239 0 R/Pg 476 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj48312 0 obj<</K 9/P 48239 0 R/Pg 476 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj48313 0 obj<</K 12/P 48239 0 R/Pg 476 0 R/S/H4/Type/StructElem>>endobj48314 0 obj<</K[13 49002 0 R 16 49003 0 R 19 49004 0 R 22 49005 0 R 25 49006 0 R 28]/P 48239 0 R/Pg 476 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj48315 0 obj<</K[29 48997 0 R 32 48998 0 R 35 48999 0 R 38 49000 0 R 41 49001 0 R 44]/P 48239 0 R/Pg 476 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj48316 0 obj<</K[45 48994 0 R 48 48995 0 R 51 48996 0 R 54]/P 48239 0 R/Pg 476 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj48317 0 obj<</A 48992 0 R/Alt(Two code definitions in a programming language. The first defines a function named 'commonNeighbour2Pair' that takes two small natural numbers and a property variable, returning a clause. It calculates common neighbors between two vertices and creates a c\lause with positive or negative literals based on a condition. The second defines a function named 'movedDimPair2' that takes a natural number, an offset, and a property variable, returning an optional clause. It filters pairs of indices and applies the f\irst function if a condition on the indices is met, otherwise returns none. The code focuses on generating logical clauses related to common neighbors in a graph or network.)/K[55 48993 0 R]/P 48239 0 R/Pg 476 0 R/S/Figure/Type/StructElem>>endobj48318 0 obj<</K[58 48990 0 R 61 48991 0 R 64]/P 48239 0 R/Pg 476 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj48319 0 obj<</K 65/P 48239 0 R/Pg 476 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj48320 0 obj<</K[1 48988 0 R 4 48989 0 R 7]/P 48239 0 R/Pg 479 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj48321 0 obj<</A 48986 0 R/Alt(A function named "encodeDiameter2_complete" takes two inputs: a small letter c of type assignment n, and a small letter auxOffset of type nat. Inside the function, a variable hd2 is defined as the result of converting the graph of the assignment c to a si\mple graph. The function returns true if the assignment agrees with the graph hd2 and if evaluating the CNF formula for encoding diameter 2 with auxOffset is true. This expression checks if the assignment c correctly encodes a diameter-2 property in the g\iven graph structure.)/K[8 48987 0 R]/P 48239 0 R/Pg 479 0 R/S/Figure/Type/StructElem>>endobj48322 0 obj<</K 11/P 48239 0 R/Pg 479 0 R/S/H3/Type/StructElem>>endobj48323 0 obj<</K[13 48983 0 R 16 48984 0 R 19 48985 0 R 22]/P 48239 0 R/Pg 479 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj48324 0 obj<</A 48981 0 R/Alt(Table showing a triangular number pattern where each row starts with dashes and ends with consecutive numbers increasing from 1 to 10. The first row has dashes followed by numbers 1 to 4, the second row has two dashes followed by numbers 5 to 7, the third\ row has three dashes followed by numbers 8 and 9, the fourth row has four dashes followed by number 10, and the last row has only dashes. This pattern visually represents a decreasing number of dashes and an increasing sequence of numbers arranged diagon\ally.)/K[23 48982 0 R]/P 48239 0 R/Pg 479