lus abstractions \(flat\), red dots for Twee \(flat\), and orange dots for Twee \(no flat\). All methods show increasing time with more problems solved, with the gre\en method generally solving problems faster before reaching the cutoff.  The right plot compares domain abstractions with four methods: blue dots for Twee \(no flat\), orange dots for Twee \(flat\), green dots for abstractions \(no flat\), and red dots fo\r abstractions \(flat\). The red method solves fewer problems within the cutoff, while the others perform similarly, with time increasing as more problems are solved.  These plots illustrate how different abstraction techniques affect problem-solving time\ and efficiency, emphasizing that partial proof abstractions tend to solve more problems faster compared to domain abstractions.                                              Cactus plot showing that Twee without domain abstractions solves approx. 860 prob\lems within 5 minutes with goal flattening and 870 without goal flattening, and with domain abstractions solves approx. 880 problems without goal flattening and 900 with goal flattening.\r\n␀)/K 2/P 50381 0 R/Pg 301 0 R/S/Figure/Type/StructElem>>endobj50488 0 obj<</K[3 50738 0 R 6 50739 0 R 8 50740 0 R 11 50741 0 R 14]/P 50381 0 R/Pg 301 0 R/S/Caption/Type/StructElem>>endobj50489 0 obj<</K 16/P 50381 0 R/Pg 301 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj50490 0 obj<</K 17/P 50381 0 R/Pg 301 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj50491 0 obj<</K 19/P 50381 0 R/Pg 301 0 R/S/H3/Type/StructElem>>endobj50492 0 obj<</K 21/P 50381 0 R/Pg 301 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj50493 0 obj<</K[23 50735 0 R 25 50736 0 R]/P 50381 0 R/Pg 301 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj50494 0 obj<</K[1 50734 0 R 4]/P 50381 0 R/Pg 304 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj50495 0 obj<</K 6/P 50381 0 R/Pg 304 0 R/S/P/Type/StructElem>>endobj50496 0 obj<</K[50709 0 R 50710 0 R 50711 0 R 50712 0 R 50713 0 R]/P 50381 0 R/S/L/Type/StructElem>>endobj50497 0 obj<</K 32/P 50381 0 R